## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### ❌ Complex Test Setup
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create complex test setup
const complexTestSetup = () => {
  // Complex mocking
  // Complex state management
  // Complex test utilities
};
```

### ❌ Over-Testing
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T test implementation details
it('calls setState with correct parameters', () => {
  // Testing internal implementation
});
```

### ❌ Complex Mocking
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create complex mocks
const complexMock = jest.fn().mockImplementation(() => {
  // Complex mock logic
});
```

## Simple Testing Patterns

### Component Testing
```javascript
// ✅ Test user interactions
it('displays loading state', () => {
  render(<ParticipantsList loading={true} />);
  expect(screen.getByText('Loading...')).toBeInTheDocument();
});

it('displays error state', () => {
  render(<ParticipantsList error="Failed to load" />);
  expect(screen.getByText('Failed to load')).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

### API Testing
```javascript
// ✅ Test API responses
it('creates participant successfully', async () => {
  const participantData = { name: 'John Doe', region: 'Berlin' };
  
  const response = await request(app)
    .post('/api/participants')
    .send(participantData)
    .expect(201);
  
  expect(response.body.success).toBe(true);
  expect(response.body.data.name).toBe('John Doe');
});
```

### Database Testing
```javascript
// ✅ Test database operations
it('inserts participant into database', async () => {
  const participant = { name: 'John Doe', region: 'Berlin' };
  
  const result = await executeQuery(
    'INSERT INTO participants (name, region) VALUES ($1, $2) RETURNING *',
    [participant.name, participant.region]
  );
  
  expect(result.rows[0].name).toBe('John Doe');
});
```

## Test Coverage

### Essential Tests
- [ ] **Component rendering** - Components display correctly
- [ ] **API endpoints** - Routes return expected responses
- [ ] **Database queries** - Data operations work correctly
- [ ] **Authentication** - Auth flows work properly
- [ ] **Error handling** - Errors are handled gracefully

### Non-Essential Tests
- [ ] **Implementation details** - Internal function calls
- [ ] **Complex edge cases** - Rare scenarios
- [ ] **Performance tests** - Load testing
- [ ] **Integration tests** - Complex workflows

## Benefits

- **Fast tests** - Simple tests run quickly
- **Easy maintenance** - Simple tests are easy to update
- **Clear failures** - Simple tests have clear error messages
- **Focused coverage** - Tests cover essential functionality
- **Developer friendly** - Easy to write and understand

## Test Commands

```bash
# ✅ Simple test commands
npm test                    # Run all tests
npm run test:watch         # Watch mode
npm run test:coverage      # Coverage report
```

## Remember

> "Tests are a specification that happens to be executable." - Kent Beck

**Test behavior, not implementation.**
**Keep tests simple and focused.**
**Test the user experience, not the code.**